><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mstislav of Tmutarakan was a son of Vladimir the Great who ruled the principality of Tmutarakan on the Taman peninsula.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mstislavl"><span class="enc-name">Mstislavl</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mstislavl is a small town in Mogilev Region, eastern Belarus, on the Vikhra river in the Sozh basin.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mswati-ii"><span class="enc-name">Mswati II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mswati II was king of the Swazi from 1840 to 1868, and the Swazi people take their name from him.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mtamvuna-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/mtamvuna-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mtamvuna River</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mtamvuna is a river of South Africa that flows into the Indian Ocean and forms part of the boundary between the provinces of KwaZulu-Natal and the Eastern Cape.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mthatha-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/mthatha-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mthatha River</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mthatha is a river of the Eastern Cape in South Africa, flowing south-east past the city of Mthatha into the Indian Ocean.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mthethwa-paramountcy"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/mthethwa-paramountcy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mthethwa Paramountcy</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Mthethwa Paramountcy was a Nguni state near the coast of what is now KwaZulu-N